<s-1 id="RM000001F75008X_02_0013" proc-id="RM0550J___00009SY00000">
<ptxt>Adjust Front Door Panel Sub-assembly LH</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using SST, loosen the body side bolts and adjust the door in the forward/rearward and vertical directions.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09812-00010</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B153649" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>26</t-value1>
<t-value2>265</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Loosen the door side bolts and adjust the door in the vertical direction and the front end of the door in the left/right direction.</ptxt>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>26</t-value1>
<t-value2>265</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
<atten3>
<ptxt>When adjusting, use a service bolt to adjust the fit.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a torx socket wrench T40, loosen the striker installation torx screws just enough to move the striker. Using a brass bar, lightly tap the striker to adjust the rear end of the door in the vertical and left/right directions and the front door lock striker plate assembly.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B153650" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<torque>
<torqueitem>
<t-value1>23</t-value1>
<t-value2>235</t-value2>
</torqueitem>
</torque>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
